<main class="content-block docs-page">
  <h1 class="page-title">Agent playbook</h1>
  <p class="page-lede">Machine-oriented steps to deploy the host status agent. Do not add in-app status reporters to each service.</p>

  <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation">
    <a href="/docs">Overview</a>
    <a href="/docs/agent">Agent playbook</a>
    <a href="/docs/spec">SPEC</a>
  </nav>

  <ol class="agent-steps">
    <li>Copy the collector repo’s <code>agent/</code> directory to the server (e.g. <code>/opt/odi-status-agent</code>).</li>
    <li><code>npm install</code> in that directory. Requires Node ≥ 20.17.</li>
    <li>Create <code>config.json</code> (from <code>config.json.example</code>): <code>statusReportUrl</code>, <code>statusReportKey</code>, <code>hostId</code>, <code>scanRoots</code> (array of paths). Legacy <code>config.env</code> is used only if <code>config.json</code> is missing.</li>
    <li>On the collector Configure page, allowlist this server’s egress IP.</li>
    <li>Run <code>npm run once</code> and confirm HTTP 200; dashboard shows <code>host:&lt;hostId&gt;</code> and nested apps.</li>
    <li>Install systemd timer from <code>agent/systemd/</code> (hourly) or run <code>npm start</code> as a long-lived process.</li>
    <li>Ensure Apache (if used) sets <code>X-Forwarded-Proto https</code> for the collector; agent push is outbound HTTPS to the collector and does not need Apache.</li>
    <li>Remove any in-app <code>startStatusReporter</code> / <code>STATUS_REPORT_*</code> wiring from apps on this host.</li>
    <li>Acceptance: after one hour, reports are not stale; host checks include apt/reboot + OS LTS; apps show process + connector checks + agent <code>npm_audit</code>; collector injects Node/npm LTS on apps.</li>
  </ol>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Discovery rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Walk <code>scanRoots</code> up to <code>scanDepth</code> (default 4).</li>
      <li>Any directory with <code>package.json</code> is an app (<code>node_modules</code> skipped).</li>
      <li>Connectors: probe when env keys exist in the app’s <code>config.env</code> then <code>.env</code> (Mongo via <code>MONGO_URI</code>/<code>MONGODB_URI</code>/<code>MONGO_URL</code>, HubSpot, Forecast, Moodle, Gmail/Calendar, email OAuth2/SMTP, OpenAI/AI, OAuth/session/webhook presence).</li>
      <li>Per app: run <code>npm audit --json</code> with the npm next to the app’s Node binary when known (else <code>npm</code> on <code>PATH</code>). Collector does not re-audit.</li>
      <li>Host report: OS / apt / reboot only. Node and npm are per-app (nvm-aware).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
